  <Primary><Body>
    <Part Number="2"><Title>Formation of the contract</Title>
      <P1group RestrictExtent="E+W+S+N.I." RestrictStartDate="1980-01-01"><Title>Contract of sale.</Title>
        <P1 id="section-2" DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1979/54/section/2" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1979/54/section/2">
          <Pnumber>2</Pnumber>
          <P1para>
            <P2 id="section-2-1"><Pnumber>1</Pnumber><P2para><Text>A contract of sale of goods is a contract by which the seller transfers or agrees to transfer the property in goods to the buyer for a money consideration, called the price.</Text></P2para></P2>
            <P2 id="section-2-2"><Pnumber>2</Pnumber><P2para><Text>There may be a contract of sale between one part owner and another.</Text></P2para></P2>
          </P1para>
        </P1>
      </P1group>
      <P1group RestrictExtent="E+W+S+N.I." RestrictStartDate="1980-01-01"><Title>Capacity to buy and sell.</Title>
        <P1 id="section-3" DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/1979/54/section/3" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/1979/54/section/3">
          <Pnumber>3</Pnumber>
          <P1para>
            <P2 id="section-3-1"><Pnumber>1</Pnumber><P2para><Text>Capacity to buy and sell is regulated by the general law concerning capacity to contract and to transfer and acquire property.</Text></P2para></P2>
          </P1para>
        </P1>
      </P1group>
    </Part>
